  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="3bdda842-a202-4cfa-96bf-c80303719329"><problem><para>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents \(y=(x−2)^2−8\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>2</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 2. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex is found by using the squared term of the vertex form. The value of the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is 2. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
